<p>Pernod is a type of Absinthe that can be traced all the way back to the 1790s.</p>
<p>It’s made by mixing wormwood, fennel, melissa, and anise in a neutral spirit (usually wine) in a copper alembic where the mixture is distilled to produce a transparent liquor.</p>
